{{French flags}}

The galleries below show flags of [[France]] attributed to the metropolitan [[regions of France|regions]], former regions, [[French departments|departments]], [[Overseas departments and regions of France|overseas regions]], [[overseas collectivities|collectivities]] and subdivisions. 

The official status of many regional and territorial flags in France is often unclear. Since the late 20th centuries, many regional and local authorities have adopted [[logo]]s as their primary emblems, which are subsequently displayed on [[logo flag]]s. Such flags often serve as de facto institutional symbols but usually lack formal [[heraldry|heraldic]] or [[vexillology|vexillological]] recognition.

Alongside these are numerous traditional regional flags, whose status also varies. Some historical flags date back centuries, while others are [[banner of arms|banners of arms]] or more recent designs created by private individuals or associations. In some cases, these flags have later gained semi-official or customary use through adoption by public institutions, commemorative coinage, public transport, or municipal buildings.

